Wed Aug  5 17:37:10 UTC 2026 - Jan Engelhardt <jengelh@inai.de>

- Derive from ffmpeg-8.spec
- Update to release 9.0
  * More Vulkan API acceleration work like Vulkan APV video
    decoding and Apple ProRes RAW Vulkan acceleration, the Vulkan
    v360 video filter, HE-AAC 960 decoding, a transpose NVIDIA CUDA
    filter, animated WebP decoding and demuxing, continued AMD AMF
    enhancements, more AVX-512 optimizations, and more.
  * Remove CELT decoding support (doesn't affect Opus CELT)
  * Remove CELT-in-Ogg parsing
  * avcodec/rasc: Check that 32-bit DLTA accesses stay within the row.
    (CVE-2026-58049, bsc#1269550)
  * avformat/spdifenc: bound DTS core_size against the packet size in the HD path.
    (CVE-2026-64833, bsc#1272755)
  * avformat/rtpdec_asf: reject ASF objects smaller than their header
    (CVE-2026-64834, bsc#1272757)
  * avcodec/tdsc: unref the reference frame before reallocating on size change.
    (CVE-2026-65703, bsc#Bug 1272759)
  * avformat/ty: don't let the Series2 AC3 trim underflow the packet size
    (CVE-2026-65704, bsc# 1272760)
  * avfilter/vf_floodfill: remove unneeded variables
    (CVE-2026-65705,  bsc#1272761)
  * avfilter/vf_swaprect: size the temp row buffer for the widest plane.
    (CVE-2026-65706, bsc#1272762)
  * avfilter/vf_hqdn3d: support dynamic frame sizes.
    (CVE-2026-66036, bsc#1272763)
  * avformat/iamf_parse: check count_label against the available bytes
    (CVE-2026-66037, bsc#1272764)

